{"text": " or service-based business. Why did I relocate it to that? That's where this course comes in. It's a three-part course. The foundation of it, part one, is building automation for the grind. What I mean by that, a lot of repetitive tasks, a lot of copy and paste, a lot of very time-consuming tasks that are essentially the same over and over and over. You can learn to automate those things. The second part of it is building systems around those automations. You can actually have an end-to-end workflow for your marketing department, your analytics, your marketing campaigns, the ideation of your campaigns, or for sales. You can have something like a system that I've built to where it automatically connects to Calendly. If somebody books a call, that agent in the system, it will actually put it on your calendar. It will take the email and company information. It will go enrich that data, prepare who you're going to be speaking toward, put a Slack notification, and then put it in the pipeline of whatever salesperson is actually going to do it so it can actually act as an SDR. Why did I go down that road? Why did I go down that road? Why did I go down that road? Why did I go down that road? Why did I go down that road? Why did I go down that road? Why did I go down that road? Why did I go down that road? Why did I go down that road? Why did I go down that road? Why did I go down that road? Why did I go down that road? Why did I go down that road? Why did I go down that road? Why did I go down that road? Why did I go down that road? Welcome to buildmytribe.ai I'm getting hot. Welcome to buildmytribe.ai My name is Mike, and you're here because of one of two reasons. Either you know very little about AI, but you're hearing all the hype, and you want to learn about it, or you've started to use it, but it's very basic. It's like a chat GPT, one prompt in, you get one output, and you want to really learn how to build systems around it and how powerful AI can be. from all this hype that you're hearing, but you don't have a strategic plan to learn about it, or a process to implement it into your business. That's where this course comes in. I'm going to break it down into three parts. The first part being the foundation. Automating your grind. That is repetitive tasks, things that are very time consuming. You can actually create workflows and systems that buy back your time, sometimes hours and hours of your time, that you lose every single week. You can automate that. I'm going to teach you how to do that. The second part is connecting the dots. Not just automating simple tasks or a single workflow, but having a system in place to where it does multiple tasks, to where you can have like an SDR prep a meeting for sales agents, or you can synthesize large amounts of data for your marketing team, and have AI driven results, and synthesis from marketing analysis of your Facebook ads, or your Google ads, or your cold email outreach, and then having systems that work it from end to end, and then you can create entire systems around these things. The last part is the elevation of all of it. So not just building the basic, oh, one agent does one task, or even the basics of a system, but an overall scalable system using what I call the software as a service mindset. What I mean by that is there are principles that you can actually steal from software developers, and once you understand these principles, AI will make a lot more sense to you. Software engineers, they really get AI the quickest. They've actually been using it for probably the longest, because all of them have been developing the LLMs and all that, and they're creating all of the new shiny object toys. Oh, Jesus. I need some...", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 1.74, "text": " or service-based business.", "tokens": [50365, 420, 2643, 12, 6032, 1606, 13, 50452], "temperature": 0, "avg_logprob": -0.21931605693722558, "compression_ratio": 1.6317991631799162,